<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Tolaram falls into loss at half year.</title>
<headline>Tolaram falls into loss at half year.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     14 loss     vs 23 profit</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  -	    vs  -</p>
<p>    Attrib loss	     1.60	  vs 2.64 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss	    1.63	  vs 2.64 profit</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.03	  vs  -</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   1.40	  vs 1.48</p>
<p>    Turnover		  32.47	 vs 41.83</p>
<p>Full name: Tolaram 2000 Ltd (textiles)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the downturn in the textile industry had been more severe than expected. Margins were likely to remain under pressure and second half profits were unlikely to exceed those of the year ago period.</p>
<p>The company has approved capital expenditure of 30 million rand and arrangements to raise funds for this are at an advanced stage.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
